-- title:
--   Valuation rings as local rings on a universally closed model
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a commutative ring and let $\mathrm{toBase}_0 : X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$ be a morphism of schemes with $X_0$ integral and locally Noetherian and $\mathrm{toBase}_0$ universally closed, and assume every stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X_0,y}$ is integrally closed in its fraction field (hypothesis `hn₀`). Let $F_0$ be a field equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure and let $\varphi_0 : F_0 \xrightarrow{\sim} K(X_0)$ be a ring isomorphism onto the function field of $X_0$ which is compatible with the two base maps, in the sense that for every $a \in A_0$ the element $\varphi_0(a \cdot 1)$ equals the image of $a$ under `SemistableModel.baseToFunctionField toBase₀`, namely $a$ pushed through $\Gamma(\operatorname{Spec} A_0, \mathcal{O}) \to \Gamma(X_0, \mathcal{O})$ and then germed at the generic point of $X_0$. Assume further that $F_0$ is algebraic over the $A_0$-subalgebra $A_0[t]$ generated by a single element $t \in F_0$. Finally let $O \subseteq F_0$ be a valuation subring containing the image of $A_0$ and also the inverse of $a \cdot 1$ for every $a \in A_0$ with $a \cdot 1 \neq 0$. Then there is a point $x \in X_0$ with $\mathrm{SemistableModel.localRing}\, X_0\, \varphi_0\, x = O$ as subrings of $F_0$, that is, the image of $\mathcal{O}_{X_0,x} \to K(X_0) \xrightarrow{\varphi_0^{-1}} F_0$ is exactly $O$.
--
--   This is the existence half of the classical dictionary between the valuation rings of the function field of a relative curve containing the base and the points of a normal model which is proper (here only universally closed) over the base; the valuative criterion supplies the point and normality together with the one-variable hypothesis forces the local ring to be the whole valuation ring. It is used in the construction of normal proper models, via [`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_normalProperModel_of_valuationSubrings_of_form_of_isAlgebraic_relDimOne_genComplete_henselian`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.exists_normalProperModel_of_valuationSubrings_of_form_of_isAlgebraic_relDimOne_genComplete_henselian), and relies on the maximality criterion [`Subalgebra.isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot_of_isAlgebraic_adjoin_singleton`](thm.html#Subalgebra.isMaximal_of_isPrime_of_ne_bot_of_isAlgebraic_adjoin_singleton) for nonzero primes of subalgebras of $F_0$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_exists_localRing_eq_valuationSubring_of_isIntegrallyClosed_of_universallyClosed.lean

